  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of the Early Warning System for Disaster Risk Reduction in Province of Cebu, Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cebu Province in the Philippines faces severe damage from typhoons and floods every year, but the lack of a flood early warning system makes proactive evacuation and disaster response challenging. This project aims to minimize human and property losses and enhance climate resilience by establishing flood early warning systems in 10 regions within Cebu Province. To achieve this, the project will install rainfall and water level observation stations, warning stations, and an integrated data platform, while also strengthening local operational capabilities through training programs for PAGASA and local government officials. The project is aligned with the Philippine government&apos;s disaster management policies and international agreements such as the SDGs, SFDRR, and EW4ALL, with a focus on ensuring a sustainable operational framework</narrative>
  </description>
